Never download OpenCode at runtime; use the system package.

Upstream's update service installs @opencode/cli via npm into the
user prefix when the configured binary is missing or outdated.
On openSUSE OpenCode ships as an RPM dependency, so upgrades must
flow through RPM. canUpgradeBinary reports false (the UI then hides
the upgrader) and upgradeBinary fails loudly if reached.

